H3900.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3899 (לֶחֶם)
{(for man or beast), especially bread, or grain (for making it)}
KJV: feast.

H3902.definition:
from H3899 (לֶחֶם); foodful; (or perhaps erroneous transcription) for H1022 (בֵּית הַלַּחְמִי)
Lachmi, an Israelite; or rather probably a brief form
KJV: Lahmi. See also H3433 (יָשֻׁבִי לֶחֶם).

H3903.definition:
probably by erroneous transcription for לַחְמָם; from H3899 (לֶחֶם); food-like;
Lachmam or Lachmas, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lahmam.

H3904.definition:
(Aramaic) from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a concubine
KJV: concubine.

H3905.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to press, i.e. (figuratively) to distress
KJV: afflict, crush, force, hold fast, oppress(-or), thrust self.

H3906.definition:
from H3905 (לָחַץ);
distress
KJV: affliction, oppression.

H3907.definition:
a primitive root;
to whisper; by implication, to mumble aspell (as a magician)
KJV: charmer, whisper (together).

H3908.definition:
from H3907 (לָחַשׁ);
properly, a whisper, i.e. by implication, (in a good sense) a private prayer, (in a bad one) an incantation; concretely, an amulet
KJV: charmed, earring, enchantment, orator, prayer.

H3909.definition:
a form of H3814 (לָאט) or else participle from H3874 (לוּט);
properly, covered, i.e. secret; by implication, incantation; also secrecy or (adverb) covertly
KJV: enchantment, privily, secretly, softly.

H3910.definition:
probably from H3874 (לוּט);
a gum (from its sticky nature), probably ladanum
KJV: myrrh.

H3911.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hide;
a kind of lizard (from its covert habits)
KJV: lizard.

H3912.definition:
masculine plural of passive participle of H3913 (לָטַשׁ); hammered (i.e. oppressed) ones;
Letushim, an Arabian tribe
KJV: Letushim.

H3913.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to hammer out (an edge), i.e. to sharpen
KJV: instructer, sharp(-en), whet.

H3914.definition:
a form of H3880 (לִוְיָה);
a wreath
KJV: addition.

H3915.definition:
or (Isaiah 21:11) לֵיל; also לַיְלָה; from the same as H3883 (לוּל);
properly, a twist (away of the light), i.e. night; figuratively, adversity
KJV: (mid-)night (season).

H3916.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3815 (לָאֵל)
{Lael an Israelite}
KJV: night.

H3917.definition:
from H3915 (לַיִל);
a night spectre
KJV: screech owl.

H3918.definition:
from H3888 (לוּשׁ) in the sense of crushing;
a lion (from his destructive blows)
KJV: (old) lion.

H3919.definition:
the same as H3918 (לַיִשׁ);
Laish, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Laish. Compare H3889 (לוּשׁ).

H3920.definition:
a primitive root;
to catch (in a net, trap or pit); generally, to capture or occupy; also to choose (by lot); figuratively, to cohere
KJV: [idiom] at all, catch (self), be frozen, be holden, stick together, take.

H3921.definition:
from H3920 (לָכַד);
something to capture with, i.e. a noose
KJV: being taken.

H3922.definition:
from H3212 (יָלַךְ); a journey;
Lekah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lecah.

H3923.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Lakish, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lachish.

H3924.definition:
from the same as H3883 (לוּל);
a loop
KJV: loop.

H3925.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to goad, i.e. (by implication) to teach (the rod being an Oriental incentive)
KJV: (un-) accustomed, [idiom] diligently, expert, instruct, learn, skilful, teach(-er, -ing).

H3926.definition:
a prolonged and separable form of the prepositional prefix;
to or for
KJV: at, for, to, upon.

H3927.definition:
or לְמוֹאֵל; from H3926 (לְמוֹ) and H410 (אֵל); (belonging) to God;
Lemuel or Lemoel, a symbolic name of Solomon
KJV: Lemuel.

H3928.definition:
or לִמֻּד; from H3925 (לָמַד);
instructed
KJV: accustomed, disciple, learned, taught, used.

H3929.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Lemek, the name of two antediluvian patriarchs
KJV: Lamech.

H3930.definition:
from H3886 (לוּעַ);
the gullet
KJV: throat.

H3931.definition:
a primitive root;
to deride
KJV: mock.

H3932.definition:
a primitive root;
to deride; by implication (as if imitating a foreigner) to speak unintelligibly
KJV: have in derision, laugh (to scorn), mock (on), stammering.

H3933.definition:
from H3932 (לָעַג);
derision, scoffing
KJV: derision, scorn (-ing).

H3934.definition:
from H3932 (לָעַג);
a buffoon; also a foreigner
KJV: mocker, stammering.

H3935.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
Ladah, an Israelite
KJV: Laadah.

H3936.definition:
from the same as H3935 (לַעְדָּה);
Ladan, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Laadan.

H3937.definition:
a primitive root;
to speak in a foreign tongue
KJV: strange language.

H3938.definition:
a primitive root;
to swallow greedily; causatively, to feed
KJV: feed.

H3939.definition:
from an unused root supposed to mean to curse;
wormwood (regarded as poisonous, and therefore accursed)
KJV: hemlock, wormwood.

H3940.definition:
or לַפִּד; from an unused root probably meaning to shine;
a flambeau, lamp or flame
KJV: (fire-) brand, (burning) lamp, lightning, torch.

H3941.definition:
feminine plural of H3940 (לַפִּיד);
Lappidoth, the husband of Deborah
KJV: Lappidoth.

H3942.definition:
from the prepositional prefix (to or for) and H6440 (פָּנִים);
anterior
KJV: before.

H3943.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to bend, i.e. (by implication) to clasp; also (reflexively) to turn around or aside
KJV: take hold, turn aside (self).

H3945.definition:
a primitive root;
to deride
KJV: scorn.

H3946.definition:
from an unused root thought to mean to stop up by a barricade; perhaps fortification;
Lakkum, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lakum.

H3947.definition:
a primitive root;
to take (in the widest variety of applications)
KJV: accept, bring, buy, carry away, drawn, fetch, get, infold, [idiom] many, mingle, place, receive(-ing), reserve, seize, send for, take (away, -ing, up), use, win.

H3948.definition:
from H3947 (לָקַח);
properly, something received, i.e. (mentally) instruction (whether on the part of the teacher or hearer); also (in an active and sinister sense) inveiglement
KJV: doctrine, learning, fair speech.

H3949.definition:
from H3947 (לָקַח); learned;
Likchi, an Israelite
KJV: Likhi.

H3950.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pick up, i.e. (generally) to gather; specifically, to glean
KJV: gather (up), glean.

H3951.definition:
from H3950 (לָקַט);
the gleaning
KJV: gleaning.

H3952.definition:
a primitive root;
to lick or lap
KJV: lap, lick.

H3953.definition:
a primitive root;
to gather the after crop
KJV: gather.

H3954.definition:
from H3953 (לָקַשׁ);
the after crop
KJV: latter growth.

H3956.definition:
or לָשֹׁן; also (in plural) feminine לְשֹׁנָה; from H3960 (לָשַׁן);
the tongue (of man or animals), used literally (as the instrument of licking, eating, or speech), and figuratively (speech, an ingot, a fork of flame, a cove of water)
KJV: [phrase] babbler, bay, [phrase] evil speaker, language, talker, tongue, wedge.

H3957.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a room in a building (whether for storage, eating, or lodging)
KJV: chamber, parlour. Compare H5393 (נִשְׁכָּה).

H3958.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a gem, perhaps the jacinth
KJV: ligure.

H3959.definition:
the same as H3958 (לֶשֶׁם);
Leshem, a place in Palestine
KJV: Leshem.

H3960.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to lick; but used only as a denominative from H3956 (לָשׁוֹן);
to wag the tongue, i.e. to calumniate
KJV: accuse, slander.

H3961.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3956 (לָשׁוֹן);
speech, i.e. a nation
KJV: language.

H3962.definition:
from an unused root thought to mean to break through; a boiling spring;
Lesha, a place probably East of the Jordan
KJV: Lasha.

H3963.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a measure for things dry
KJV: half homer. m

H3964.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4100 (מָה);
(as indefinitely) that
KJV: [phrase] what.

H3965.definition:
from H75 (אָבַס);
a granary
KJV: storehouse.

H3966.definition:
from the same as H181 (אוּד);
properly, vehemence, i.e. (with or without preposition) vehemently; by implication, wholly, speedily, etc. (often with other words as an intensive or superlative; especially when repeated)
KJV: diligently, especially, exceeding(-ly), far, fast, good, great(-ly), [idiom] louder and louder, might(-ily, -y), (so) much, quickly, (so) sore, utterly, very ([phrase] much, sore), well.

H3968.definition:
the same as H3967 (מֵאָה);
Meah, a tower in Jerusalem
KJV: Meah.

H3969.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3967 (מֵאָה); properly, a primitive numeral
a hundred; also as a multiplicative and a fraction}
KJV: hundred.

H3970.definition:
from H183 (אָוָה);
a desire
KJV: desire.

H3972.definition:
apparently a form of H3971 (מאוּם);
properly, a speck or point, i.e. (by implication) something; with negative, nothing
KJV: fault, [phrase] no(-ught), ought, somewhat, any (no-)thing.

H3974.definition:
or מָאֹר; also (in plural) feminine מְאוֹרָה; or מְאֹרָה; from H215 (אוֹר);
properly, a luminous body or luminary, i.e. (abstractly) light (as an element); figuratively, brightness, i.e.cheerfulness; specifically, a chandelier
KJV: bright, light.

H3975.definition:
feminine passive participle of H215 (אוֹר);
something lighted, i.e. an aperture; by implication, a crevice or hole (of a serpent)
KJV: den.

H3976.definition:
from H239 (אָזַן);
(only in the dual) a pair of scales
KJV: balances.

H3977.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3976 (מֹאזֵן)
{(only in the dual) a pair of scales}
KJV: balances.

H3978.definition:
from H398 (אָכַל);
an eatable (includ. provender, flesh and fruit)
KJV: food, fruit, (bake-)meat(-s), victual.

H3979.definition:
from H398 (אָכַל);
something to eat with,i.e. a knife
KJV: knife.

H3980.definition:
from H398 (אָכַל);
something eaten (by fire), i.e. fuel
KJV: fuel.

H3981.definition:
from H553 (אָמַץ);
strength, i.e. (plural) resources
KJV: force.

H3982.definition:
from H559 (אָמַר);
something (authoritatively) said, i.e. an edict
KJV: commandment, decree.

H3983.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3982 (מַאֲמַר)
{something (authoritatively) said, i.e. an edict}
KJV: appointment, word.

H3984.definition:
(Aramaic) probably from a root corresponding to H579 (אָנָה) in the sense of an inclosure by sides;
a utensil
KJV: vessel.

H3985.definition:
a primitive root;
to refuse
KJV: refuse, [idiom] utterly.

H3988.definition:
a primitive root;
to spurn; also (intransitively) to disappear
KJV: abhor, cast away (off), contemn, despise, disdain, (become) loathe(some), melt away, refuse, reject, reprobate, [idiom] utterly, vile person.

H3989.definition:
from H644 (אָפָה);
something baked, i.e. a batch
KJV: baken.

H3990.definition:
from the same as H651 (אָפֵל);
something opaque
KJV: darkness.

H3991.definition:
prolonged feminine of H3990 (מַאֲפֵל);
opaqueness
KJV: darkness.

H3992.definition:
a primitive root;
to be bitter or (causatively) to embitter, i.e. be painful
KJV: fretting, picking.

H3993.definition:
from H693 (אָרַב);
an ambuscade
KJV: lie in ambush, ambushment, lurking place, lying in wait.

H3994.definition:
from H779 (אָרַר);
an execration
KJV: curse.

H3995.definition:
from H914 (בָּדַל);
a separation, i.e. (concretely) a separate place
KJV: separate.

H3996.definition:
from H935 (בּוֹא); (with or without H8121 (שֶׁמֶשׁ))
an entrance (the place or the act); specifically sunset or the west; also (adverb with preposition) towards
KJV: by which came, as cometh, in coming, as men enter into, entering, entrance into, entry, where goeth, going down, [phrase] westward. Compare H4126 (מוֹבָא).

H3997.definition:
feminine of H3996 (מָבוֹא);
a haven
KJV: entry.

H3999.definition:
from H2986 (יָבַל) in the sense of flowing;
a deluge
KJV: flood.
